### Health check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/health

### About check
GET http://localhost:8080/api/about

### GET all tickets
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets

### Get one existing ticket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/6a50650ad0e1026b90eb03bd

### Get one missing ticket
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets/000000000000000000000000

### create new valid ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Cannot access email",
  "description": "User cannot login to company email account.",
  "category": "Email",
  "priority": "HIGH",
  "createdBy": "amir@example.com"
}

###create an invalid ticket
POST http://localhost:8080/api/tickets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": "",
  "category": "",
  "priority": "",
  "createdBy": ""
}

###query for status "OPEN"
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?status=OPEN

###query for priority "HIGH"
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?priority=HIGH

###query for category "Email"
GET http://localhost:8080/api/tickets?category=Email

###all endpoints are working fine.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 3. Register a normal user - should return token with role USER
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Normal User",
  "email": "user@example.com",
  "password": "User@12345"
}

### login as admin
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@example.com",
  "password": "Admin@12345"
}

